                <pb facs="0195" n="97" sameAs="frus:frus1930v02/pg97"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/10774: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-03-26T11:00:00+08:00">March 26, 1930—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received March 26—3:10 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>222. My 208, March 21, 11 a.m.<anchor n="78" xml:id="d55-f1"/> Following from
                    American Consul General at [Hankow]: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“March 25, 11 a.m. The Steamship <hi rendition="#italic">Ifung</hi> of
                            Yangtze Rapid Steamship Company was fired on at mileage 219 above Hankow
                            from the right bank by about 400 soldiers carrying a red flag with white
                            sun. The soldiers fired about 700 shots from rifles. An armed naval
                            guard on the <hi rendition="#italic">Ifung</hi> [returned?] the fire
                            with 272 rounds. One enlisted man slightly wounded in left forearm by
                            ricochet fragment. Heavy firing was heard inland at mileage 220 above
                            Hankow.</p>
                        <p>There is no unusual military activity in evidence here at present, and,
                            so far as can be learned, local authorities are depending on Government
                            forces now in north and northwest Hupeh and along the Pinghan Railway in
                            Honan to defend Hankow if the threatened war materializes.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
